W5 — Link navigation, attention line, footer, and g guide (0.4.0)

Date: 2026-11-22
Version: 0.4.0 (with libtam 0.9.0)

SUMMARY

- Added shared core module `tam_pager` (`include/tam_pager.h`,
  `src/tam_pager.c`) to `libtam` 0.9.0 for attention-line/link SGR,
  safe OSC 8 open/close, standard Tamlinux footer formatting, URI
  classification, percent-decoding, local path resolution, heading
  slugification, and shell-free `xdg-open` dispatch.
- Extended `tam-view` Markdown and HTML renderers to record sidecar
  link spans (including wrapped multi-word links, table links,
  autolinks, and entity-decoded HTML `href`) and anchor targets
  (Markdown heading slugs with deduplication, HTML `id` and `<a name>`).
- Added mode-aware attention line to `tam-view` pager: active on
  rendered Markdown and HTML (`Down`/`Up` steps links and rows with
  auto-highlighting; `Right`/`Enter`/`o` follows `#anchor`, local files,
  or `xdg-open`; `Left`/`Backspace` returns via history stack;
  `Tab`/`Shift-Tab` jumps between links), while plain text / raw mode
  and standalone Mermaid keep direct `Down`/`Up` viewport scrolling.
- Updated footer to `<file path> | L<n> <top>-<bot>/<total> v0.4.0`
  (or `<top>-<bot>/<total>` in non-attention mode, `?` for streaming or
  >4 MiB files).
- Added `g` keybindings-guide toggle (scrollable on short terminals;
  `Home`/`<`/`1g` go to line 1; `Ng` goes to line N).
- Added `--hyperlinks[=auto|always|never]` / `--no-hyperlinks` for
  optional OSC 8 hyperlinks, omitted on `TERM=linux`, `TERM=dumb`,
  `--no-color`, `NO_COLOR`, and redirected stdout by default.

